# traces/MANIFEST.sha256 - digests of the generated trace sets (SW §5.6). The data is not in git:
# every set is regenerated byte-identically by its regen.sh from fixed seeds (`traces/<set>/regen.sh
# build/dev`). A set's digest is the sha256 of `sha256sum` over its files (regen.sh and Python caches
# excluded) in byte-order path order; check one with
#   cd traces && find <set> -type f ! -name regen.sh ! -path '*/__pycache__/*' -print0 | LC_ALL=C sort -z | xargs -0 sha256sum | sha256sum
# The digests are those of the dev host: the generator draws some random inputs through libm
# (normal deviates, the ROPE constants), so another libm may give different bytes.
# A frozen reference set goes into git once the ISA is frozen for the RTL.
# set           files  digest
m2              1211   a1a4fa60eee1b9aed01908a4e608d95f99856c550ab416ad4abc7fbda523d7cb
gen             557    04b1cae61cef8cac19806c560ce35b01c4f4e2cf649e7b94dd5cc32e9a66704f
vu              1757   27fe7775a5dc7773e6874756eb8080290b15ea76eaaa2d119cfd642800e39ca3
at              4066   b8964f172df4c4bc6b9affe5375545c6f4bddb24a3ff816a56a1579912caa7a5
ctrl            5811   dc1e307d27ab5f636138739eee3d63cb1e95d2bef62481879846b34af0e0a71c
m3              5104   8bc7ae77bb740880826433a0a7b91218bc3080d4e60e1a39fa917756d00e57a7
model-v1conv    3140   b294781e83e56be8f2d9a84f325d718f7b9482126b1fffc6f33d3832ac99d6c6
